# Bracket — Project Overview

Tournament management system: React SPA + FastAPI REST API + PostgreSQL.

## Repo Layout

```
backend/         Python FastAPI API + business logic (uv)
frontend/        React 19 SPA (Vite 8, pnpm)
docs/            Next.js 16 + Nextra documentation site
docker-compose.yml  Combined image + Postgres
Dockerfile       Combined backend+frontend image
run.sh           Local dev: frontend + backend together
```

## Tech Stack

| Layer       | Tech                                                      |
|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| Backend     | Python 3.12+ / FastAPI / SQLAlchemy Core / Alembic        |
| Frontend    | React 19 / TypeScript 5.9 / Vite 8 / Mantine 8           |
| Database    | PostgreSQL (async via databases + asyncpg)                |
| Auth        | JWT Bearer (HS256, 1-week expiry), bcrypt, hCaptcha       |
| Data fetch  | SWR (reads), Axios (writes), OpenAPI-generated TS types   |
| i18n        | i18next (12 languages, Crowdin sync)                      |
| Docs        | Next.js 16 + Nextra 4 + Tailwind 4                       |
| Package mgr | uv (Python), pnpm (Node)                                 |

## Architecture

Three-tier SPA + REST monolith, deployable combined or split.

Backend layers: `routes/ → logic/ → sql/ → schema.py`
Frontend layers: `pages/ → components/ → services/ → openapi/`

OpenAPI-first contract: backend generates spec → frontend generates TS types.

## Key Conventions

- All backend routers use `APIRouter(prefix=config.api_prefix)`, tags set in `app.py`
- Response wrappers: `SuccessResponse` for mutations, `DataResponse[T]` for reads
- Frontend uses `@openapi` for types only, hand-written Axios+SWR for HTTP calls
- All user-facing strings go through i18next (`useTranslation()`)
- ID types are branded `NewType` aliases (e.g. `TournamentId`, `TeamId`)
- Timestamps use `heliclockter.datetime_utc`, not stdlib datetime

## Git Workflow

- `master` tracks upstream `evroon/bracket`
- `dev` branch for our feature work
- Upstream remote: `upstream` (https://github.com/evroon/bracket.git)

